  "confidence": 0.3,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "open_connection",
      "components": ["U3"],
      "pins": ["U3.2"],
      "nets": ["unconnected-(U3-EN-Pad2)"],
      "observed": "The TPS62933 buck converter (U3) has its EN pin (pin 2) marked no_connect. The netlist gives it no net, so nothing drives or pulls the enable input.",
      "expected": "The EN pin of a buck regulator should be tied to a defined level, through a divider or pull-up to VIN, or driven by the controller. Leaving it floating makes the enable state undefined unless the part has an internal pull-up, which the netlist does not show. The specification does not describe EN as left open.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(net (code \"142\") (name \"unconnected-(U3-EN-Pad2)\") (class \"Default\") (node (ref \"U3\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"EN\") (pintype \"input+no_connect\")))"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "U1 (TPS62933) ... 24 V → 5 V synchronous buck regulator, 3 A"}
      ],
      "impact": "If EN is not pulled up internally, the 5 V rail may fail to start or may start unreliably. That would take down the ESP32 supply, the LDO and everything downstream.",
      "confidence": 0.3
    },
    {
      "category": "wrong_value",
      "components": ["R4", "T7", "T5"],
      "pins": ["R4.2", "T7.1"],
      "nets": ["+3V3", "/NET0035"],
      "observed": "R4 is a 10k resistor from +3V3 to the T7 (IRLR2905) gate net /NET0035. That net also has the T5 collector and the R31 100 Ω drive from IO10. The gate is therefore pulled high by default, and the main-pump FET is switched on whenever T5 is not pulling the gate low.",
      "expected": "A pump MOSFET gate should default to the off state, with a pull-down, or the gate should be otherwise defined so the pump cannot run during boot or when the controller is floating.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(node (ref \"R4\") (pin \"2\") (pintype \"passive\"))"},
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(node (ref \"T7\") (pin \"1\") (pinfunction \"G\") (pintype \"passive\"))"},
        {"source": "spice", "quote": "R4 /NET0035 +3V3 10k"}
      ],
      "impact": "The main circulation pump may energise at power-up or while the ESP32 GPIOs are floating, because the gate sits high unless the T5 pre-driver actively holds it low.",
      "confidence": 0.2
    }
  ],
  "summary": "Two candidate issues are reported with low confidence: the TPS62933 enable pin is unconnected, and the main-pump FET gate has a 10k pull-up to +3V3 that could energise the pump by default. The rest of the power, I2C, isolation, stepper and sense networks match the netlist and SPICE deck, so the verdict is weak."
}

